WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.640
July 2017 saw the release — and immediate
embrace of Spider-Man's MCU reboot, which

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.460
featured Tom Holland as New York's friendly
neighborhood wall-crawler.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:15.240
In 2018, we got to see another dimension to
the franchise literally in the animated masterpiece

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.400
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.340
"Hey — are you OK?"

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:21.700
"No, I'm not."

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.260
"What's going on with your body?"

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.220
"I don't think my atoms are real jazzed about
being in the wrong dimension."

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.520
The film introduced multiple Spidey characters,
including Brooklyn teen Miles Morales and

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.360
Gwen Stacy, the Spider-Woman of her universe
who is known to fans as Spider-Gwen.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.080
Quick-witted, confident and able to pull off
an impromptu haircut, Stacy's battle skills

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.340
and warm heart made her an instant fan favorite.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.680
Into the Spider-Verse wasn't Stacy's first
appearance on the big screen, but it was the

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.620
first time we saw the character with powers.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:55.410
She was played by Bryce Dallas Howard in 2007's
Spider-Man 3, the last movie in the Tobey

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:00.151
McGuire-starring trilogy; she had a bigger
role in the Andrew Garfield franchise, in

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.040
which she was played by Emma Stone.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.900
But these versions of Gwen are based on the
canonical Spider-Man, in which spoiler alert

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.100
she dies tragically.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.620
Spider-Gwen, however, first appeared in the
comics in 2014 and got her own series in 2015.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.250
She lives in an alternate universe where she
was bitten by the radioactive spider instead

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:23.070
of her best friend Parker, and she later fails
to save him giving her a similar guilt-tinged

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.080
motivation to her mainstream counterpart.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:26.100
Powers?

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:26.820
Check.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.200
Sad origin story?

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.020
Check.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.280
Sense of humor and heart?

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.100
Check.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.720
But will Spider-Gwen ever get her own movie?

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.540
"See you around, Spider-Man."

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.580
While there are no firm plans to give Spider-Gwen
her own live-action solo film at this moment,

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.960
it's safe to say that there's never been a
better time at the cinema for female superheroes.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.600
After years of being left out or relegated
to the background, these characters are finally

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.180
seeing their names in lights.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.720
In 2017, DC's Wonder Woman became the highest-grossing
superhero origin story ever.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:09.660
It was surpassed in 2019 by Captain Marvel,
the MCU's first film centered on a female

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:10.220
superhero.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.040
We know there will be a Captain Marvel 2 coming
along within the next few years, and we're

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.909
also getting movies focused on Black Widow
and a female Thor played by Natalie Portman

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:21.640
in the MCU's Phase 4.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.620
On the small screen, Disney+ will be offering
up the WandaVision series, which focuses on

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:30.340
Scarlet Witch, and two more about Ms. Marvel
and She-Hulk.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:36.140
More immediately, we can get our damsels in
no distress fix at the cinema, via DC's anti-heroine

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.040
Harley Quinn in Birds of Prey.

00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:43.720
The creators of Into the Spider-Verse drew
on the ideas of Marvel mastermind Stan Lee,

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.240
who always liked Spider-Man because he could
be anyone under the mask.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.820
They were able to get audiences pumped about
Spideys who weren't necessarily white, male,

00:02:51.829 --> 00:02:57.019
or... well, human, and with their newfound
emphasis on showcasing female heroes, it feels

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.620
like the time is right for Stacy to take center
stage.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.760
We aren't the only ones who want to see more
Spider-Gwen.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.160
Rumors have abounded that Marvel parent company
Disney is very keen on the character, and

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:13.060
that Marvel wants her to have her own solo
MCU movie which might also connect to a potential

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.800
film based on the Young Avengers.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.540
And, you know what?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.220
We might already have seen her.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:22.459
Eagle-eyed fans watching Avengers: Endgame
at home spotted a student at Peter Parker's

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:27.080
high school with blonde hair, a pink backpack
and a skirt with a spiderweb design.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.699
The MCU has already sneaked in a reference
to Spider-Verse hero Miles Morales in Spider-Man:

00:03:32.699 --> 00:03:37.780
Homecoming, when Aaron Davis played by Donald
Glover mentions that he has an unnamed nephew,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.790
who was confirmed to be Miles in a deleted
scene.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.260
"Yeah, sorry Miles…

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.420
I'm not gonna make it.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.020
Yeah, I'm just stuck."

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:50.380
Whether we get to see a live-action version
of Stacy onscreen or not, it's all but certain

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.300
that she'll be back in animated form.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.659
Into the Spider-Verse did quite well at the
box office, and even beat out Incredibles

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.280
2 for the Best Animated Feature Oscar.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.980
This promptly led to the greenlighting of
a sequel which will further explore Miles

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.320
and Gwen's relationship, and we're also getting
an animated spin-off led by Stacy.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.700
That film will feature an all-female team
of superheroes, including Jessica Drew — the

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:17.320
main continuity's Spider-Woman — and Cindy
Moon, AKA Silk.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.240
All of this bodes well for Stacy's live-action
fortunes, and while we don't know exactly

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.450
when or how it will happen, we're pretty sure
she won't be leaving all of the web-slinging

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.120
to the boys for much longer.

